{
 "note": "R122c - position split of the skater style codes per distinct source (the method Spike S4 used to confirm player-style.toml on\nNHL Legacy): companion style (exhibitionskaterai p_style / playerstyle) x bio position (0 C, 1 LW, 2 RW, 3 D - position confirmed by\nroster line slots in R120c), joined by game_id. Per code: defenceman / forward counts and the side it belongs to (>= 0.9 share), so the\ndefence code set and forward code set of each title can be compared with player-style.toml (D 1..4, F 5..10) and the NHL 07 synthetic\nvocabulary (D 1..2, F 3..7). A split is title-owned structural evidence about which codes are defence roles; it does not name them.\nUsage: python r122c_style_position_split.py <out.json>\n",
